  "findings": [
    "The ending row order is B-only followed by A-and-B. Row0’s actual near and far triples are both tail images, preserving its endpoint B. Row1 inherited near triples are old images ending at the retained A, while its far triples remain tail images because the full top interval still ends at B. The code uses these exact distinct identities.",
    "The extra A gate uses tripleLift_upper, the exceptional adjacent pair in middle/upper positions. The actual near triple is (old Y,A,B), with Y the last core child’s left endpoint; the actual far triple is (I.left,A,B). Their free lower positions collapse to Y and the fixed core left endpoint X0, respectively, giving (tD(Y)−tH(X0))/2.",
    "The body reuses the exact rational cutGateProduct and reindexes all row0 gates by endingInteriorZeroEquiv. Row1 is reindexed by Unit plus all inherited core gates, whose Unit branch is exactly A. Product splitting yields one additional factor times the entire core gate product, with no missing or duplicated gate.",
    "No existing gate or child value is divided out. Empty core interiors, zero gates and unary core compositions are included; in the unary case Y can equal X0. No immediate-predecessor identification is assumed at this gate stage. The general helper includes all actual source ending intervals without n≥4 or extra geometric restrictions."
  ],
